Z||000000||tomanyfieros||08-10-2001||11:50 PM||||i thought it would be neat to post this while i have lots of time on my hands, my dad has bilt a "TA Truck" and no it is not computer made, or anything like that. It is an 89 Trans Am on an RV frame, that is being made into a car hauler....This thing was started in like 1990, and everyone who has seen it, says they have never seen anything like it." it is a one of a kind!" i will have pics soon, <BR>heres what happened<BR>89 Trans Am cut behind the door (about a 1/2 foot) and took 4 truck backs (where the rear window is) and made them a one and put it on there, it has ttops, and has a cummins engine in it, tilt front end, and is the neatest thing in Ohio, it will have every option in it, like digital gauges, ect. it has about 1000 hours in making it to the point it is at, it was sitting in the basement when the house caught on fire, and it has not been worked on sense, (1997 is when the house caught fire) i will try to have pics soon, i thought this would make someone interested and come look at it and buy fiero Parts... lol, not really but if anyone wants to come look at it, they are more than welcome to, I am in Athens Ohio, on route 50 <BR>75984 US Hwy 50<BR>Albany Ohio 45710<BR>it runs and drives.... neat as he!! and i want to drive it someday.... pics will be soon, i need to keep this towards the top so i can find it easier. and does anyone want to post the pics for me? i will have the pics by sunday, and can email u the pics and have them posted.... any help? Thanx Jason<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dreamer.gif">    <BR><B>We all have dreams, but not everyone gets them...</B>||||reg||1
